OnePlus 15 OxygenOS 16.0.9.400-r1 TWRP installer
===================================================

This ZIP contains the exact matched kernel images validated on CPH2747 running
@FIRMWARE@:

  payload/boot.img
    bytes: @BOOT_BYTES@
    sha256: @BOOT_SHA256@

  payload/system_dlkm.flatten.ext4.img
    bytes: @SYSTEM_DLKM_BYTES@
    sha256: @SYSTEM_DLKM_SHA256@

The installer is deliberately firmware-specific. Do not flash it on OOS
16.0.8.300, a different OOS build, or an untested device variant.

Requirements
------------

* An unlocked OnePlus 15 already using a validated Infiniti TWRP build that
  provides /system/bin/twrp-flash-kernel and lpdump.
* A clean snapshot state. The installer refuses an active OTA merge/snapshot.
* Writable decrypted /sdcard or mounted external storage. A recovery-rootfs
  /sdcard placeholder is rejected because it cannot retain backups across a
  reboot. The installer backs up active-slot boot and system_dlkm before any
  write.
* system_dlkm on the active slot must be at least @SYSTEM_DLKM_BYTES@ bytes.
  The stock OOS layout is smaller. From TWRP, reboot to fastbootd and run:

    fastboot getvar current-slot
    fastboot getvar snapshot-update-status
    fastboot resize-logical-partition system_dlkm_b @SYSTEM_DLKM_BYTES@

  Replace `b` with the `a` or `b` value reported by `current-slot` (do not
  include the underscore used by Android's slot-suffix property).

  Only resize when snapshot-update-status is none and the super partition has
  enough free space. If fastbootd rejects the resize, stop and resolve the
  device's dynamic-partition/OTA state; do not use lpadd against live super.

What it does
------------

* Detects the recovery boot slot and writes only boot_<slot> and
  system_dlkm_<slot>.
* Verifies archive payload hashes, image headers, ext4 format, logical
  metadata, input sizes, target backups, and post-write readback hashes.
* Flashes matching system_dlkm first and boot second.
* Leaves system_dlkm_oki, vendor_boot, vendor_dlkm, dtbo, and VBMeta untouched.

The installer does not disable AVB verification or flash VBMeta. It is for the
same unlocked, test-only AVB configuration used to validate release
@RELEASE_TAG@. It is not a production AVB-secure installation method.

After a successful install, reboot System without changing slots. The recovery
helper reports the backup directory and verifies both writes before returning.
